<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lelang Commandery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">108 BCE–313 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lelang was a Chinese commandery set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> in 108 BCE after its conquest of Gojoseon, with its centre near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyongyang">Pyongyang</a>. For four centuries it was a channel for Chinese culture, writing and trade into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, and its tombs have yielded fine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lacquerware">lacquerware</a> and other luxury goods. Goguryeo conquered it in 313.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lelang-commandery.jpg" alt="Lelang Commandery" width="320" height="501" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Asieon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Early_4th_century_Lelang_Commandery.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
